    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d882">

                <pb facs="0705" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12967.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-23T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 23, 1914, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This morning an opportunity was presented to ask the President regarding the
                    relations with Zapata. He replied that nothing has been arranged. I understood
                    that in the attempts so far there has been a lack of confidence on each side.
                    The President intimated that possibly the good offices of the United States
                    might be effective in arranging a conference with Zapata and himself. It is a
                    delicate matter but should not be very difficult if handled with proper
                    intelligence, discretion and tact.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
